                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          %h2#axioms_of_universes Axioms of universes
          %p
            Just as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZFC"} ZFC
            and other material
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theories
            may be augmented with axioms guaranteeing the existence of
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+universe"} Grothendieck universe
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ETCS"} ETCS
            and other structural set theories be augmented with axioms guaranteeing the existence of universes in the above sense. For example, the counterpart of Grothendieck’s axiom
          %ul
            %li
              For every set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              there exists a universe
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              containing
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\in U
          %p would be
          %ul
            %li
              For every morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\colon A \to I
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi el
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} el\colon E \to U
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              is
              = succeed "-small." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          %h2#consequences Consequences
          %p
            One can show, from the above axioms, that the
            = succeed "-small" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+object"} quotient object
          %h2#in_terms_of_indexed_categories In terms of indexed categories
          %p
            Recall that an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+category"} indexed category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudofunctor"} pseudofunctor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}^{op}\to \Cat
            = succeed "-indexed" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            %em self-indexing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔼
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{E}
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I\in \mathcal{E}
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+category"} slice category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔼
                    %mi I
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{E}^I = \mathcal{E}/I
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\colon I \to J
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^*
          %p
            An
            %strong internal full subcategory
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is a full sub-indexed category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔽
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔼
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{E}
            (that is, a collection of full subcategories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mi I
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔼
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}^I\subset \mathbb{E}^I
            closed under reindexing) such that there exists a generic
            = succeed "-morphism," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔽
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi el
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} el\colon E \to U
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}^U
            such that for any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\colon A \to I
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}^I
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ≅
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi el
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \cong f^*(el)
            for some
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon I \to U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+category"} locally cartesian closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇉
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1 \;\rightrightarrows\; U
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔽
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}
            is equivalent, as an indexed category, to the indexed category represented by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1 \;\rightrightarrows\; U
          %p
            An internal full subcategory is an
            %strong internal full subtopos
            if each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔽
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logical+functor"} logical
            subtopos of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔼
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{E}
            (closed under finite limits, exponentials, and containing the subobject classifier). A universe in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            = succeed "-small" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          %h2#in_the_internal_logic In the internal logic
          %p
            In a topos with a universe, we can talk about small objects in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            by instead talking about elements of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi el
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} el\colon E \to U
            interpreted as a “family of objects”
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi u
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi u
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S_u)_{u\colon U}
          %ol
            %li
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_u
              (in the sense that there exists an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ↪
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi u
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \embedsin S_u
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              such that
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ≅
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \cong S_v
            %li
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              such that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≅
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(S_u) \cong S_v
            %li
              there is a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_v
              is
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty
            %li
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              and all functions
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi u
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon S_u \to U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              such that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨄
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %msub
                            %mi S
                            %mi u
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≅
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \biguplus_{i\colon S_u} S_{f(i)} \cong S_v
          %p
            In a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-pointed+topos"} well-pointed topos
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ETCS"} ETCS
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+element"} global element
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          .query
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike
              \: I haven’t actually checked anything in this section, but it seems probable.
