                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object+classifier+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} object classifier in an (infinity,1)-topos
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+universe"} Grothendieck universe
          %h2#references References
          %p The construction of universes in presheaf toposes was first discussed in the following short note which might serve as a concise introduction to the more general reference that follows:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Hofmann"}> Martin Hofmann
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Streicher"} Thomas Streicher
              %em Lifting Grothendieck Universes
              , ms. University of Darmstadt (unpublished). (
              %a{:href => "http://www.mathematik.tu-darmstadt.de/~streicher/NOTES/lift.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p The general case is considered here:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Streicher"}> Thomas Streicher
              ,
              %em Universes in Toposes
              , pp.78-90 in L. Crosilla, P. Schuster (eds.),
              %em From Sets and Types to Topology and Analysis: Towards Practicable Foundations for Constructive Mathematics
              , Oxford UP 2005. (
              %a{:href => "http://www.mathematik.tu-darmstadt.de/~streicher/NOTES/UniTop.ps.gz"}> ps
              ,
              %a{:href => "http://www.mathematik.tu-darmstadt.de/~streicher/NOTES/UniTop.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              Christian Maurer,
              %em Universes in Topoi
              , pp.285-296 in F. W. Lawvere, C. Maurer, G. C. Wraith (eds.),
              %em Model Theory and Topoi
              , LNM
              %strong 445
              Springer Heidelberg 1975.
